    "context": "Native RR interval pid_t decoding and task-before-output errors: 998 root/UID1000 checks per architecture, including 960 guarded OTHER queries, 32 real RR interval queries and six final state/guard controls. Six PID targets, seven raw word forms, ten output forms and genuine musl wrapper calls. Original 520 failures, corrected and identical-ELF Linux 6.12.51 references zero. Linux timespec duration is scheduler/configuration dependent; references require normalized nonnegative OTHER and positive RR intervals, while native controls retain zero OTHER and 5ms RR. Two warmed 200-cycle query cohorts keep all slabs/large pages flat. Four captured fresh production builds plus two identical-C comment rebuilds, one query prototype/body delta, six-case corrected native profiles, eight host test files, unchanged allocation allowance failures, compiler/source/ELF pins and independent lifetime review. No new allocation, scheduler mutation, cross-task permissions/races, glibc, translated/ELF32 or broad roadmap completion is claimed.",
